Z||000000||Wildcat||07-08-2001||02:52 AM||||Where oh where can I find the fancy molded rubber tube that goes from the breather at the front left of engine com[artment to the throttle body intake on an 86 SE 2,8 litre,<BR>Finally got the engine for my son's car, 3.1 litre with iron heads from a Lumina Van.  Rebuilt locally for $1500 cdn.  Install is going great, no glitches or surprises and I expect to have the car running tomorrow as it is now ready to raise the cradle into the chassis.  Only trouble is this dam fancy tube is tore.  It has a steel engine breather line that connects to it as well.<BR>Thanks<BR>Tim||||reg||1
Z||000001||West Coast Fiero||07-08-2001||04:27 PM||||If you find that you cannot get one, It may make more sense to go with one of our Cold Air Intake tubes. It would be a gain in performance and it would delete the parts your looking for.<P>Eric - West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <BR>310-305-4111<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||07-09-2001||07:51 AM||||mine broke off at the end. I just ran a piece of fuel line from the valve and used a hose clamp to hold it on the nipple under the intake. Been there for years now. Its a little tite to work it thru, may need a right angle needlenose to help.<P>never mind, I was thinking you meant the small tube, not the air intake<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 07-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||stsmithgt||07-09-2001||09:51 AM||||I've bought one for about 60.00 at the dealership.  I was throwing money at my car awhile ago and picked one up.  I couldn't find one at the wrecking yard and mine was torn from the motor mounts letting the engine move too much.  It's all fixed now, but throwing money at your car can be hazardous.  Your car might develope a hunger for money like mine did and take a lot more out of your pocket.  Confusing it with aftermarket parts seems to slow down it's hunger.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||Wildcat||07-09-2001||11:00 AM||||Oh this car was money hungry looooooooooong before!<BR>My son's car and I am the lucky guy who gets to pull wrenches on it.  Went through two used 2.8's and had the same problem repeatedly, blown cranks.  Last night we just completed a 3.1 conversion and new struts/shocks.  2k cdn later its out of the shop, will be doing break-in runs today as this is a completely rebuilt engine.  Our tube was tore due to broken bracket that holds the dogbone, caused too much shifting.  Its tore about 2 inches in front of the throttle body.  I repaired it with some custom stretched exhaust pipe and a couple clamps for now.  Dealer here says it no longer available.  Our wreckers (2) won't touch a fiero! Wish I could say the same due to the time it takes to do things like engine swap etc. but no such luck.  Well at least we have a motor with decent warranty now, and the smiles I saw when the engine fired make it worth while!<BR>Tim||||reg||1
